==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Fried Shrimp Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Roe Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Essentially [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]] for Red enemies, this cat is very useful to stop the advancement of [[Bore]], [[One Horn]], [[Shy Boy]] and other Red enemies, as it can soak up damage from them while simultaneously weakening them. Use Sushi Cat on stages with lots of Red enemies for a tactical advantage.

Sushi Cat can even be used to great effect against [[Two Can]] and [[Berserkory]], as many stages feature these enemies almost by themselves, so it's possible to tank them with this near-immovable wall. Do note that when these enemies are brought along as support, having a tough defensive unit will only cause them to miss attacks less often, which can be a problem if there are units without any type of wave resistance. Another thing that improves it is its range, or lack thereof, allowing it to protect nearly all DPS units, even rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Yukimura]].

This cat is used in specific [[Cat Combo]]s such as [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] and [[Bento Special (Combo)|Bento Special]]. Cool Japan will grant your units a 15% attack power buff, and Bento Special will grant you 500¢ at the beginning of a stage. With these 2 Combos combined, your units can be much more powerful and turn the battle in your favor. Since Sushi is a part of each of these Combos, bringing them both to Red stages such as [[Growing Red]] or [[Boiling Spring]] will provide you a great advantage over your enemies.

It forms a great synergy with [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], in which one stalls the enemies while the other freezes them.

==='''True Form'''===
Roe Cat has a truly massive health pool, reaching an impressive 300k health against Reds just at level 30 (effectively over 600k with weaken)! This may seem high, but that's a necessity if this Cat wishes to stay relevant later on, which is definitely the case. Roe can and should be used in any stage that features exclusively Red enemies, at least in a specific wave or as the only relevant threat, but its use is greatly lowered when it has a chance of receiving plenty of hits from non-Reds. Even then, Roe is able to be a decent generalist tanker, provided you have plus levels. When [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] is unlocked, it synergises with Sushi Cat well.

Roe Cat also benefits greatly from boost, as a level 50 Roe can reach over '''1 million''' health against weakened reds.

==='''Talents'''===
Roe was always somewhat expensive, despite being worth its cost most of the time. Its Cost Down [[Talents|Talent]] reduces its cost by a little less than a third, but it is recommended to keep it at level 5 due to certain [[Restriction Stage|Restrictions]]. With Defense Buff, Roe Cat is also made way more viable by improving its health even further, making it not only worth bringing in far more Red-heavy stages, but even in many other stages too, acting as a more spammable, but weaker [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]]. Attack Buff, Resist Slow and Resist Freeze are situational and likely not worth the NP.

==='''Orb'''===
Tough Effect Up: Red is your best bet. Defense Up is also a good idea if you don't have it.

