==Trivia==
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Sushi Cat the ability to [[Weaken]] [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Sushi Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Grocery Cart (Removed Combo)|Grocery Cart]] and [[Triggermen (Removed Combo)|Triggermen]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Sushi Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Sushi Cat
A Cat that moves fast by spinning.
The fresh meat can take a beating. (Area Attack)
Resistant to Red, might weaken enemies.</pre>
<pre>Fried Shrimp Cat
A Cat that moves fast by spinning.
Also got into Rock 'n' Roll (Area Attack)
Resistant to Red, might weaken enemies.</pre>
<pre>Roe Cat
Don't get all salty just because you'll lose!
Eggs-elent defense and Area Attack.
Resistant to Red, might weaken enemies.</pre>
*Fried Shrimp Cat's Japanese name, Regent Cat, does not refer to monarchy, but rather the pompadours stereotypically worn by delinquents, which is also known as the [[wikipedia:ja:リーゼント|Regent style]].
*Roe Cat's Japanese description includes a pun on "イクラ". In the context of the sentence, it can mean that Roe Cat is willing to be anyone's opponent as many times as they want if they become an enemy. However, another possible meaning of the word is salmon roe, which is on Roe Cat's heads.
*The Fried Shrimp Cat with sunglasses resembles [[wikipedia:DJ Ozma|Nao Baba]]'s persona in the rock band [[Kishidan Collaboration Event|Kishidan]], [[Sho Ayanokoji (Special Cat)|Sho Ayanokoji]], while the Roe Cat with sunglasses looks somewhat like one of his other personas, DJ Ozma.

